                <pb facs="1002" n="902" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg902"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">467.11/726: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Istanbul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-11-21T12:00:00+02:00">November 21,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. From Shaw. “Secretary General Ministry of Foreign Affairs tells me informally
                    that at meetings to take place at Angora in a few days Turks will propose lump
                    sum claims settlement of $500,000. In answer to my question he said that he
                    thought there were only one or two small Turkish claims against the United
                    States.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
